<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernest II, Duke of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1818">1818</a>–<a href="/years/1893">1893</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernest II was Duke of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a> from 1844 and the elder brother of Prince Albert, husband of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a>. A liberal and supporter of German unification, he backed the German national movement and sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1866. He was also a composer and patron of music and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ernest-ii-duke-of-saxe-coburg-and-gotha.jpg" alt="Ernest II, Duke of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha" width="320" height="507" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ghémar Frères studio · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ernest_II,_Duke_of_Saxe-Coburg-Gotha_(1818-93)_circa_1863.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
